        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>In an unwelcome surprise, the FCC has placed all foreign-made routers on the so-called Covered List, effectively banning new products from sale within the United States.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The decision follows the FCC\u2019s National Security Determination, which concluded that routers used by homes and home offices could be attacked by foreign actors. As a result, \u201crouters produced in a foreign country\u201d will be added to the Covered List. That means, in effect, no future routers manufactured in a foreign country will receive FCC licenses to be sold in the United States.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>And the Covered List has teeth. At one time, products manufactured by Huawei, <a href=\"https://www.pcworld.com/article/403242/huawei-matebook-13-review-a-powerful-gpu-and-whiskey-lake-chip-propel-this-compact-notebook.html\">such as this Matebook laptop</a>, were sold in the United States. <a hre",
